.\" cr-deploy(1) manpage — mdoc format
.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt CR-DEPLOY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cr-deploy
.Nd deploy to CapRover from the terminal, by digest, and check it worked
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar COMMAND
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
drives a CapRover captain from the terminal: it reads the cluster,
registers apps, deploys images, follows builds, and rolls back.
.Fl h
and
.Fl -help
print usage and the list of commands.
.Pp
It logs in with the
.Cm caprover
CLI's saved token at
.Pa ~/.config/configstore/caprover.json
and writes a refreshed token back in the same shape. The password is
asked for in the terminal, used once, and never stored.
.Pp
Images deploy by digest only. CapRover can keep serving a stale image
after a redeploy of the same tag, so a tag is never trusted. An image
named
.Sy img-captain--*
is also accepted: those are the captain's own builds, one tag per
version, and are never reused.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width 24n
.It Cm info
The captain: version, system information, and the cluster summary as
JSON.
.It Cm nodes
The cluster's nodes, one per line: node id, type, IP, state, hostname.
.It Cm apps Op Ar NAME
Apps with their node, storage, domains, and image. Secrets are hidden.
Storage reads
.Sy volume ,
.Sy bind ,
or
.Sy NONE
from the app's volumes and its bind mounts. A bind mount is a host
folder mounted through the dashboard's Service Update Override; it is
read out of the override's TaskTemplate and survives a full replace.
With
.Ar NAME ,
one app is printed in full: port, instances, forceSsl, websocket
support, domains, volumes, bind mounts, and hidden env. An app with no
volume and no bind mount draws a warning that a redeploy starts with an
empty disk.
.Fl -json
emits the same fields as JSON, plus a
.Sy keeps_data
flag.
.It Cm ensure Ar FILE Op Fl -dry-run
Create or converge one app from an instance file.
.Fl -dry-run
prints the diff and stops. A key the file leaves
out keeps its live value, because the captain's update is a full
replace: the live definition is posted back with only the named keys
changed, so overrides such as bind mounts survive. With
.Ev CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
set,
.Nm
also points the domain's DNS at the captain.
.Pp
Instance files are YAML with the keys
.Sy app ,
.Sy node
.Po a node id, or
.Sq none
to let Swarm place it
.Pc ,
.Sy domain ,
.Sy https ,
.Sy port ,
.Sy instances ,
.Sy force_ssl ,
.Sy websocket ,
.Sy description ,
.Sy volumes ,
.Sy env ,
.Sy env_from_environment ,
.Sy env_remove ,
.Sy dns .
.It Cm deploy Ar FILE Ar TAR Oo Fl -verify Ar URL Oc Oo Fl -expect Ar KEY=VALUE Oc Oo Fl -health Ar URL Oc
Build a source tarball on the captain. The app name comes from the
instance file; the tarball is uploaded and built on the captain, and the
build log is followed to its end.
.Ev GIT_HASH
is recorded with the build.
The
.Fl -verify , -expect
and
.Fl -health
checks work as for
.Cm deploy-image .
.It Cm deploy-image Ar NAME Ar IMAGE@sha256:...
.Op Fl -verify Ar URL
.Op Fl -expect Ar KEY=VALUE
.Op Fl -health Ar URL
Deploy a pinned image. A tag is refused. With
.Fl -verify
and
.Fl -expect ,
or
.Fl -health ,
the app is polled for up to 300 seconds after the build, and the exit
status is non-zero if it never answers.
.Fl -verify
takes a JSON URL to poll.
.Fl -expect
takes the
.Sy KEY=VALUE
that URL must answer.
.Fl -health
takes a URL that must answer 200.
.It Cm rollback Ar NAME
Run the version before the current one again. The newest version older
than the running one is redeployed by its digest.
.It Cm logs Ar NAME
The last build log.
.It Cm wait Ar NAME
Follow a running build to its end. Exits non-zero when the build fails.
.It Cm delete Ar NAME Op Fl -volumes
Remove an app. It asks first, and the app name must be typed to confirm.
With
.Fl -volumes ,
the app's named volumes are deleted too.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width 36n
.It Pa ~/.config/configstore/caprover.json
The
.Cm caprover
CLI's token store. Read for the machine's base URL and token, and
rewritten with a refreshed token after login. Mode 600.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width 24n
.It Ev CAPTAIN_NAME
The CapRover machine to act on. Defaults to
.Sy captain-01 .
.Ev CAPROVER_NAME
is read as well, and takes effect when
.Ev CAPTAIN_NAME
is unset.
.It Ev CAPROVER_URL
Base URL for a machine that is not in the token store.
.It Ev CAPROVER_PASSWORD
The captain password. When unset, it is asked for in the terminal.
.It Ev CAPROVER_OTP_TOKEN
The one-time code for a captain with two-factor turned on.
.It Ev CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
When set,
.Cm ensure
points the domain's record at the captain.
.It Ev GIT_HASH
Recorded with a
.Cm deploy
build.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss Read the cluster
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cr-deploy info
cr-deploy nodes
cr-deploy apps
cr-deploy apps web --json
.Ed
.Ss Deploy an app
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cr-deploy ensure web.yml --dry-run
cr-deploy ensure web.yml
cr-deploy deploy web.yml build.tar
.Ed
.Ss Deploy an image and check it
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cr-deploy deploy-image web registry.example.com/web@sha256:1f2e... \\
  --verify https://web.example.com/version --expect version=3.2.0
cr-deploy deploy-image web registry.example.com/web@sha256:1f2e... \\
  --health https://web.example.com/healthz
.Ed
.Ss Roll back
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cr-deploy rollback web
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr caprover 1 ,
.Xr docker 1
